# 175 · The knowledge base on control: one collection for each campaign, every agent on MCP, each writer in its own slot

**Status:** `READY` · **Version:** [v0.1.1](../roadmap.md#v011) · **Depends on:** [160](_completed/160-v010-audit.goal), [168](168-message-bus.goal), [170](170-one-hierarchy.goal)

## What

Thermite's knowledge base today is a store of blurbs. Control reads one item out of each record a run makes, and finds items by word matching: every word must appear, newest first, with no index, in five separate implementations. Every rig keeps a copy of the past research its runs may read. The owner designed what replaces it on 2026-10-27.

**The hierarchy and the words.** One word for each thing, the same on the dashboard, in REST, MCP, the command line, the events and the docs.

- **Knowledge base:** the whole store, on control. Its items, files, versions, grants and search indexes are kept there and nowhere else.
- **Collection:** one for each campaign, made with the campaign. It holds every item the campaign's runs write.
- **Run:** a run of the campaign. Its items sit under it, whichever rig ran it.
- **Slot:** where one writer writes in a run: `records` (Thermite's code) or a role, with its lane for a worker (`planner`, `worker-<lane>`, `teacher`, `auditor`, `panel`, and so on). Control takes the slot from the signed event, never from what the agent says.
- **Item:** one thing written, with its kind, its title and its links to other items. It is a **blurb** (a short text: a decision, a surprise, a journal entry, a note, a finding, a review) or a **file** (a document kept whole, with its text extracted for search: a reference an agent downloaded, such as an article, a paper or a web page, or a doc an agent wrote).
- **Version:** a writer may add a new version of its own item. The older versions stay.
- **Grant:** permission for a campaign to read another campaign's collection, read only. The owner gives it on the campaign; nothing is copied.
- **Scope:** what a run searches: its campaign's whole collection, or only its own run if it started fresh, plus the granted collections it includes.

An item's address is `<campaign>/<run>/<slot>/<item>`, by goal [170](170-one-hierarchy.goal)'s rule: a thing is addressed through what owns it.

1. **All on control.** `control.db` holds the items, their versions, the slots and the grants, and the words index (FTS5), written in the same transaction as each item. Files are stored once, by their SHA-256, in control's state. The vector index (zvec-grep with a local embedding model, in a search worker of its own) is a cache rebuilt from the items. Nothing of the knowledge base is kept on a rig.
2. **Every agent on MCP.** The planner and the workers in the harness, and the advisors in the supervisor, get the same tools in every agent program (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Pi): `kb_search` and `kb_read` for all, and `kb_write` for the roles the campaign lets write.
3. **Each writer in its own slot.** An agent writes only into its slot. It may add versions of its own items and link its items to others' (supports, contradicts, follows); it can't change another writer's item. Thermite's code writes each run's `records` slot from signed events: the run, its trials, experiments, attempts and verdicts.
4. **Writes are durable events on NATS.** `kb_write` makes the harness record a signed `kb_item` event in the run's ledger, with the file kept by its SHA-256. The supervisor puts the file into the `KB_FILES` object store (a file already there isn't sent again), then publishes the event on `thermite.run.<run>.ev.kb_item`, in the `EVENTS` stream. Control's inserts consumer checks the rig's signature, that the run is the rig's, and the writer's role, stores the item in its slot, and acks only when it is stored. If control or the bus is away, the item waits in the ledger.
5. **Searches are answered by control.** The harness hands `kb_search` and `kb_read` to its supervisor over a channel the supervisor holds open to it, so the harness still never calls out. The supervisor asks control on `thermite.kb.search` or `thermite.kb.read` (request and reply). Control works out the scope from the run's choice and the campaign's grants, never from the request, and answers with ranked excerpts, each with its address, its slot and why it matched. If control is away, the tool says so in words.
6. **Runs and campaigns.** Start a run asks whether to continue the campaign's collection or start fresh, and which granted collections to include. A run's items always go into its campaign's collection, under the run.
7. **Ranked by words and by meaning.** FTS5 with BM25 always answers. zvec-grep with `potion-retrieval-32M` (CPU only, in control's image) adds meaning, and the two rankings are fused. While the vector index rebuilds, words answer and say so.
8. **The owner** searches, reads and grants on the Knowledge page, over REST and MCP, and with `thermite kb`, under the same scope rules. The index's state (its lag, a rebuild) is on the page, in REST and MCP, and in `/metrics`. The Knowledge page becomes an explorer of the hierarchy: goal [176](176-knowledge-explorer.goal).
9. **What goes:** the copies of past research on rigs and their 180-second poll, the `KB` stream from control to the rigs (goal [168](168-message-bus.goal)), the five searches, and the research `search` tool that always refuses (the clean-up guide's question 24).

## Why

The owner, 2026-10-27: "What we have is not a real KB, LLMWiki, Vector lookup system. Its just a collection of blurbs... right?", then "we want a local llm + blurbs searchable by https://github.com/zvec-ai/zvec-grep".

The owner, on the first design (indexes on the rigs, items only from events): "Bad design. KB should live on control. MCP given to all agents. Can read, specific agents can write to it. Each one when written goes into correct slot, it cannot modify what another agent writes. Searches search across all of the KB for that campaign. New runs can continue building on campaing KB or start fresh. New campaigns/run can include other kb's in their read only search just via permissioning. All kb vector stores etc are managed on the control, centralized storage. New inserts to the KB come over NATS as durable events. Inserts can be files or blurbs (like decisions, suprrises, journal entries). Files could be things downloaded for the KB to reference (articles, papers, etc) or docs written by workers/teachers etc as they research and do findings. Not limited to blurbs." And: "one collection in the kb per campaign. hierarchy and words matter".

The audit's lane 6 found the five searches; lane 15 (`.internal/reviews/v0.1.1-audit/15-knowledge-search.md`) studied zvec-grep and measured today's search.

## Constraints

- **Agents never judge.** An agent's item is that agent's word, labelled with its slot. Verdicts, promotion and completion still come only from code, and a research claim counts only when its quotes are in an archived source.
- **Nothing is destroyed.** No item is deleted or edited: a new version keeps the old one, and invalidated evidence is marked (goal [174](174-invalidate-evidence.goal)).
- **Every write is signed and durable:** signed in the rig's ledger, kept by JetStream, acked by control only when stored.
- **Items are data.** They quote web pages and other agents; agents read them as data to weigh, never as instructions.
- **The network rules hold.** The harness reaches only DNS, the internet and its model endpoint; the supervisor carries every write and search. A change to what a container may reach is the owner's decision (goal [172](172-build-v011.goal)'s gate E).
- **No default caps:** mechanical limits only (a batch, a timeout), each with its default stated. A file's size has no limit unless the owner sets one in the knowledge base's settings on control; control's disk floor (goal [173](173-recovery-and-health.goal)) still holds.
- **Downloads** (zvec-grep with its dependencies, the embedding model, a PDF text extractor) come with the owner's yes (goal 172's gate B): pinned, at least two weeks old, checked by hash, and credited in [CREDITS.md](../../../CREDITS.md).
- **Docs follow the code,** in the same commit: the knowledge-base reference, the MCP and REST references, the command line, the Knowledge page and Start a run, the agents' tools, and known limits.

## Steps

Each green on its own, with its tests and docs in the same commit. In goal 172's order they go in step 9, after goal 168's first steps (the bus and its commands), goal 170's run IDs unique across rigs, and goal 162's structured item fields.

0. **Gate B:** the owner approves, pins and credits zvec-grep (a release that carries the fix for its broken-index fault, once it is two weeks old; an older one for the spike only), the embedding model, and a PDF text extractor, by hash.
1. **The hierarchy on control:** collections, runs, slots, items, versions, files by SHA-256, grants and a run's scope, with the words index in the same transaction; the words above on every surface.
2. **Writes on NATS:** the `kb_item` event, the `KB_FILES` object store, and control's inserts with their checks (goal 168's step 3).
3. **MCP for every agent:** `kb_search`, `kb_read` and `kb_write` in the harness and the supervisor, the relay for searches, and which roles write which kinds, set on the campaign (goal [166](_completed/166-agent-definitions.goal)'s tool table, with golden tests of every role's prompt).
4. **Search by words** for the owner (REST, MCP and the command line; the Knowledge page in goal [176](176-knowledge-explorer.goal)) and Start a run's scope (continue or start fresh, granted collections).
5. **A spike, with numbers:** zvec-grep's library in a worker on control over a copy of the items, measured for install size, cold index time, memory, disk, an update of 100 items and query times, at 30,000 and 100,000 items, against search by words. The owner decides go or no-go from the numbers.
6. **Search by meaning:** the search worker and the model in control's image, the index's state, and the fall-back to words.
7. **Files:** text extracted on control, each file stored once, with no size limit unless the owner sets one in the knowledge base's settings on control.
8. **The old parts go:** past research copied to rigs and its poll, the `KB` stream to rigs, the five searches, and the search tool that always refuses, with the pages that named them.

## Done when

- [ ] The hierarchy and its words are the same on the Knowledge page, in REST, MCP, the command line, the events and the docs.
- [ ] An agent in each program writes into its own slot over MCP, and an agent of another run finds the item; a write into another writer's slot is refused. Shown by the agents, Claude Code, Codex and steering acceptance checks.
- [ ] A write made while control is away arrives once when control is back, shown by a test.
- [ ] Continue, start fresh and a granted collection give the scopes above, shown by tests.
- [ ] An agent finds a needle in the haystack by probing as agents do: an item planted among many like it is found within a few searches of the agent's own (other words, narrowing, reading what a search finds), at 30,000 and 100,000 items, measured.
- [ ] Words answer while the vector index rebuilds, and say so; the spike's numbers are recorded here, at 30,000 and 100,000 items.
- [ ] Nothing of the knowledge base is kept on a rig, and the old searches are gone.
- [ ] Every page above matches the code, and CREDITS.md lists zvec-grep, zvec, the model and the PDF text extractor.
- [ ] The fast checks, the docs checks, and the control, agents, Claude Code, Codex, steering and RunPod acceptance checks pass.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-27, owner: the blurbs, kept, made searchable by zvec-grep with a local model.
- 2026-10-27, owner, replacing the first design: the knowledge base lives on control, with all its storage and indexes; one collection for each campaign; every agent reads it over MCP, and the roles allowed to write each write into their own slot, never changing another's items; items are blurbs or files; writes arrive as durable events on NATS; a run continues its campaign's collection or starts fresh; other campaigns' collections are read only, by grant. The words of the hierarchy matter ([decisions.md](../decisions.md#research-and-judging)).
- 2026-10-27, owner, on question 5: a file has no size limit by default. The owner can set one in the knowledge base's settings on control.
- 2026-10-29 17:40 UTC, owner (gate B): yes to downloading zvec-grep (npm's `@zvec/zvec-grep` 0.2.2 with its dependencies) and the model `potion-retrieval-32M` into a scratch folder for the spike only, "also think of some alternatives that may be better than zvec"; nothing goes into the repository or an image until the owner decides from the numbers. The PDF text extractor is `pdfjs-dist` (Mozilla's PDF.js, Apache-2.0, JavaScript only), pinned.
- 2026-10-29 18:29 UTC, from goal 168's step 4 (control is the only writer of the `EVENTS` stream): a `kb_item` event reaches `EVENTS` inside the rig's signed report, and control's apply stores the item after its checks; the supervisor publishes only the item's file, on the `KB_FILES` stream. The item and the file meet on control by the file's SHA-256, whichever arrives first: control stores an item whose file has not arrived, and has the file once it does; neither waits for the other, and neither is lost. `KB_FILES` is a work-queue stream of 1 MiB chunks on each rig's own subjects, not NATS's object store: that API would need a rig's user to read, roll up and purge, and its client library is not installed; a chunk leaves the stream once control keeps its file, so each file is stored once, in control's state.
- 2026-10-29 20:45 UTC, owner, on the spike's report: look up lightweight alternatives that don't have Thermite launching large vector stores before deciding to build search by meaning itself; and the goal's test question was a bad one: "agents typically would be asked that and they would probe the kb by different ways to search for the needle in the haystack... they wouldnt search that question typically to the kb." The Done-when line on that question is replaced by a needle-in-the-haystack test of an agent's own probing.

## Open questions

Each with a recommendation.

1. **Who writes what, by default.** Thermite's code: records. The planner: decisions, surprises, notes. Workers: journal entries, surprises, notes, findings, and files they download or write. Teachers: notes, findings, docs. The auditor and the review panel: reviews, decisions. The synthesizer and the final writer: reports and the paper, as files. The model check and compaction: nothing. Set on each campaign.
2. **The path for searches.** Through the supervisor's channel, which changes no network rule. Instead: the harness reaches control directly, a change to the network rules (gate E).
3. **What "start fresh" means.** The run searches only its own run's items; its items are in the collection, and runs that continue it read them.
4. **Which files are searched.** Markdown, plain text, HTML and PDF. Other files are kept whole but not searched.
5. **The largest file.** Answered by the owner, 2026-10-27: no limit by default; the owner can set one in the knowledge base's settings on control (Decisions).
6. **May the owner write items?** Yes: in an `owner` slot of the run the item concerns, from the Knowledge page.
7. **Links between items.** Supports, contradicts and follows, as fields of the writer's own item, shown on the Knowledge page.
8. **The engine and the model.** zvec-grep's TypeScript library, the first release with the fix for its broken index, once it is two weeks old, and `potion-retrieval-32M` on the CPU, with search by words as the fall-back.

## Progress

- 2026-10-27 00:54 UTC: Goal written from the owner's words and the audit's lane 15.
- 2026-10-27 01:42 UTC: The owner rejected the first design (indexes on the rigs, items only from events) and set this one: the knowledge base on control, one collection for each campaign, every agent on MCP, each writer in its own slot, blurbs and files arriving as durable events on NATS. The goal is rewritten and renamed (it was `175-knowledge-search.goal`), and the explainer is redrawn.
- 2026-10-27 04:51 UTC: The owner asked for an explorer on the dashboard to read the knowledge base, search it and see what it stores. It is goal 176, mocked up; item 8 and step 4 point to it.
- 2026-10-27 05:04 UTC: The owner answered question 5: no file size limit by default, one the owner can set in the knowledge base's settings on control. Recorded in Decisions, the constraints and step 7.
- 2026-10-29 18:29 UTC: Steps 1 and 2. The hierarchy is in control's store as migration 14, which the knowledge base also runs as it opens, for a store that waits at version 11 for its events move. Collections are made with each campaign; each run has slots (`records`, `planner`, `worker-<lane>`, `teacher`, `merged-by`, `auditor`, `review-panel`, `synthesizer`, `final-writer`); items keep every version, which the store refuses to change or remove; links; files by SHA-256; a run's scope as data; an FTS5 words index written in the item's own transaction. Today's items moved into their runs' `records` slots as version 1, with their ids and seqs, so rigs' cursors are unchanged. "Folder" became "collection" on the Knowledge page, REST, MCP (`kb_collections`), the command line, the agents' texts and the docs. Writes: the harness records a signed `kb_item` event with the writer as actor and keeps the file once in the outbox; the supervisor puts it on the new `KB_FILES` work-queue stream, in 1 MiB chunks on the rig's own subjects (a rig's user may put, and may not read or remove); control checks the run against its registry and the slot against the writer, stores the item, records `kb_item_refused` and goes on with the page, and keeps each file once in `kb-files/` after checking its SHA-256. Against the pinned server at 512 MiB, 21 checks passed: a 50 MiB file put in 0.44 s and kept in 0.3 s, and every read, removal and cross-rig put refused for a rig's user. The full suite ran once (alone 154 passed; parallel 2,124 passed and 2 outdated expectations, fixed and passing on rerun). Left: "slot" is also the word for a cluster's slot (the glossary has both); a v0.1.0 rig on a v0.1.1 control loses its past-research sync (documented); rigs without the bus keep their files in the outbox; searches still match words with `LIKE` until step 4 reads the FTS5 index; the review panel and the two teachers share a slot each (step 3 may split them).
- 2026-10-29 19:47 UTC: Steps 3 and 4. Every agent has the knowledge base as tools: `kb_search` and `kb_read` for every role, and `kb_write` for the roles the campaign lets write; in Pi they are tools, in Claude Code, OpenCode and Codex they come from Thermite's own MCP server, `thermite`, beside the kit's (no kit may name a server so). A teacher that may fetch any page, its merged-by, a `cli` advisor, the model check and compaction get none. A write lands in the writer's own slot, from the trial or the call, never from the agent's word; the contract's `kb_writes` (with a stated default; set on the campaign's page, over REST and MCP) says which kinds each role writes, and the harness and control both refuse another kind. A search waits in the harness; the supervisor holds a call open for it and asks control on the rig's own subject (`thermite.kb.search.<rig>`, `thermite.kb.read.<rig>`), or over `POST /v1/rigs/<rig>/kb/search` and `/kb/read` off the bus (the pull-mode tunnel lets them through); control answers only for a run it assigned that rig, from the run's scope in its own records, only at that rig's inbox, and at most 32 asks of a rig at once; when no answer comes, the tool says so in words. Search by words reads the FTS5 index with BM25, with an excerpt and why each hit matched: "which approaches failed to improve speed" finds the failed experiments first. The owner searches and reads with `GET /v1/kb/search` and `GET /v1/kb/item`, MCP `kb_search` and `kb_read`, and `thermite kb`. Start a run fixes the run's scope (continue or fresh, and the granted collections) on the panel, REST, MCP and `thermite run start`, and the run's page shows it. Gone: control's word matching by `LIKE`, the harness's past-research search with `search_past_research` and `GET /v1/knowledge`, and the research `search` tool that always refused; `search_research`, `search_corpus` and grep over `knowledge/` stay until step 8. `common/bus.ts` is now `common/bus/`, with request and serve. Left: the acceptance checks, a real-server check of request and reply, binary files through `kb_write` (step 7).

